.TH NVR-VIEWER 1 "2026" "nvr-viewer 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nvr-viewer \- video wall for up to 16 ONVIF network cameras
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nvr-viewer
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Discovers ONVIF cameras on the local network via WS\-Discovery and displays
their RTSP streams in a grid of up to 16 tiles. Decoding is delegated to
libmpv, with hardware acceleration when available.
.PP
Grid tiles use each camera's lowest\-resolution profile (substream); the
high\-resolution profile is used only when a tile is zoomed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-user " " \fIUSER\fR
ONVIF username.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-password " " \fIPASSWORD\fR
ONVIF password. Prefer the configuration file to avoid exposing it in the
process list.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-timeout " " \fISECONDS\fR
WS\-Discovery wait time. Default 4.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interface " " \fIIP\fR
Local address used to send the multicast probe. Useful with several NICs.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-subnet " " \fICIDR\fR
Subnet scanned when multicast discovery returns nothing.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-cameras " " \fIFILE\fR
JSON file describing cameras manually.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-discovery
Skip ONVIF discovery entirely.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-scan
Do not fall back to a TCP scan of the subnet.
.TP
.B \-\-layout " " \fIN\fR
Initial tile count: 1, 4, 9 or 16.
.TP
.B \-\-list
Print discovered cameras and their stream URIs, then exit.
.TP
.B \-\-write\-config
Create a default configuration file and exit.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.BR 1 ", " 2 ", " 3 ", " 4
Switch to 1, 4, 9 or 16 tiles.
.TP
.BR Left ", " Right
Previous / next page of cameras.
.TP
.B Double click
Zoom a tile and switch it to the high\-resolution stream.
.TP
.B Esc
Leave zoom or fullscreen.
.TP
.B F11
Toggle fullscreen.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/nvr-viewer/config.json
Credentials and defaults. Should be mode 0600.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mpv (1)
